## 1. Definitions and covered rights

**Licensor** means the natural person publishing as **yidewen**
(GitHub account: `chenxuanwu107-cell`), only to the extent that person holds
or is authorized to grant the rights expressly covered by this License.
This identification does not claim copyright in unprotected material or rights
owned by third parties.

**Skill** means the R01 Requirements Engineering and R02 Engineering Coordination
& Handoff skill definitions and the original prompts, templates, documentation,
and code expressly designated as covered in the adopted release's rights
manifest. It includes modifications only to the extent they contain protectable
expression from the covered material. It excludes third-party material and
Ordinary Work Products. A directory name or a citation does not make third-party
content the Licensor's property.

**Individual** means a natural person acting in that person's own capacity.
**Organization** means a corporation, company, partnership, association,
unincorporated organization, institution, government body, or other organized
entity. A company remains an Organization even with one shareholder, employee,
or director. An employee, officer, agent, or contractor acting as an
Organization's operator does not become an eligible Individual merely by using
a personal account or device.

**Independent Professional Use** means an Individual's own commercial work,
including freelancing, independent development, consulting, and personal
business projects, subject to Section 3. A business/trading name alone does not
disqualify the Individual if the activity is legally that same natural person's
activity and no Organization receives operation or control of the Skill.
Registration, unlimited liability, or sole ownership alone does not establish
eligibility. A registered unincorporated enterprise acting in its own name is
not automatically the Individual; ambiguous cases need separate written
clarification from the Licensor before operational use.

**Ordinary Work Products** means independently delivered task results such as
application code, requirements documents, designs, analyses, and project plans
that do not contain the Skill or a substantial protected reproduction of it,
and do not give access to its operation. A deliverable is not excluded merely
because the Skill helped create it or because it describes general ideas or
methods. Copying protected prompt instructions, source code, template text, or
their substantial protected adaptations into a deliverable does not turn them
into Ordinary Work Products. Substantiality depends on applicable law and the
actual expression, not a fixed word count or similarity score.

**Operational Use** means deploying, running, invoking, integrating, or using the
Skill as executable or model-facing instructions, including through an agent,
IDE, API, automation, or hosted service. Ordinary reading of public material is
addressed separately in Section 6.

## 2. Individual grant

Subject to these terms and only to the extent of rights the Licensor can grant,
an eligible Individual receives a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
non-transferable copyright license to read, study, research, copy, run, and
privately modify the Skill for personal projects and Independent Professional
Use. The Individual may earn income without revenue sharing, an income ceiling,
or a separate fee under this License. This is not a patent or trademark grant.

The Individual may create and sell or deliver Ordinary Work Products to any
lawful customer, including Organizations. The customer may use, modify,
commercialize, sell, and license those Ordinary Work Products under its
agreement with the Individual, subject to applicable third-party rights. This
License places no downstream field-of-use restriction on Ordinary Work Products
and claims no ownership of them merely because the Skill was used.

## 3. Independent services for organizational customers

An Individual may accept paid projects from an Organization only while all of
the following remain true:

1. The Individual independently holds, operates, and controls the Skill in the
   Individual's own capacity and personally controlled environment.
2. The customer may define the desired work, provide lawfully usable materials,
   review progress, set deliverable requirements/deadlines, and receive Ordinary
   Work Products. Payment and ordinary project oversight alone do not grant
   the customer use or control of the Skill.
3. The customer receives neither the Skill nor substantial protected copies of
   it, credentials or runtime access to it, nor the ability to deploy, invoke,
   schedule, operate, administer, integrate, or control it.
4. The arrangement supplies the Individual's professional judgment and ordinary
   deliverables, not access to Skill functionality. An organizational API,
   self-service portal, unattended request queue, shared agent, or equivalent
   operational interface to the Skill is not permitted by this exception.
5. The Individual does not place the Skill under the customer's enterprise
   account, managed workspace, execution environment, or operational direction,
   or otherwise serve as a proxy operator of the customer's Skill capability.

These conditions are a license eligibility test, not a determination of tax,
employment, agency, or labor-law status. A contract label alone is insufficient.
Long-term or on-site work is not automatically prohibited or permitted; actual
capacity, control, environment, and the working relationship must satisfy this
Section. If that cannot be established, no operational permission is presumed.

## 4. No organizational operational license; no circumvention

Except under a separate written license from the Licensor, an Organization is
not granted Operational Use, directly or indirectly. In particular, this License
does not permit:

- Internal deployment for development, management, research, or production,
  including noncommercial organizational operations.
- Employees, officers, or agents operating the Skill in their organizational role.
- Corporate API calls, agents, IDE integrations, CI/CD, SaaS, shared automated
  workflows, or organization-managed allocation of Skill capability.
- Transfer, sublicensing, white-labeling, commercial mirrors, repackaging, or
  hosted access to the Skill for an Organization.
- Using personal accounts, contractors, intermediaries, third-party hosting, or
  nominally independent arrangements to achieve these prohibited uses.

Receiving Ordinary Work Products under Section 3 is expressly permitted and is
not prohibited indirect use. General-purpose tools do not themselves become
the Skill. An eligible Individual may submit the Skill to a computing
or model provider solely to perform that Individual's permitted task. To the
extent the Licensor actually holds the necessary rights, the provider and its
necessary personnel/sub-processors receive a non-exclusive permission
limited to the transmission, copying, inference, task storage, security/abuse
handling, legal compliance and retention/deletion acts necessary for that task,
within the actual applicable product terms and controls documented as fitting
this grant. The provider may charge for its general computing/model service;
that alone is not a sale or sublicense of the Skill.

This permission is for technical processing, not independent use of
the Skill for the provider's own professional work, resale, deployment as a
reusable Skill service, unrelated training or general product improvement. It
does not authorize an enterprise customer to access, invoke or control the
Skill, and cannot be used to disguise a customer's proxy-operated capability.
The Individual must retain actual account and task control; a customer-managed
workspace, customer key or customer Skill API remains outside this exception.

No provider is deemed compatible merely because the account is personal,
training is disabled, the product has a particular name, or the client is local.
No blanket exemption applies to Codex, ChatGPT, APIs or other providers. If the
actual mandatory terms require broader rights, the submission needs separately
approved rights-holder permission or a different agreement/product/execution
route before it is made. This License cannot narrow a provider's agreement,
bind a non-assenting provider or authorize rights the Licensor does not hold.
Shared GPTs/plugins, marketplace publication, third-party apps and other
additional recipients require separate review. The product-specific analysis
and unverified conditions are recorded in [Cloud processing](legal/CLOUD_PROCESSING.md).

## 5. Personal modifications, sharing, and contributions — S2

Eligible Individuals may privately modify the Skill for permitted uses and may
noncommercially copy and share the Skill and protected modifications with other
eligible Individuals under this same License, preserving the license text,
attribution, provenance and applicable notices. Identify modifications; do not
claim inherited validation or endorsement. Each eligible recipient receives
rights directly from the Licensor subject to this License, not a sublicense
from the sender. The non-transferability in Section 2 does not prevent this
expressly permitted same-license sharing.

No permission is granted to charge for the Skill itself, commercially host its
functionality, white-label it, offer runtime access, or sublicense it on other
terms. Organizations receive no project Operational Use grant through sharing.
Applicable platform rights and mandatory law remain separate under Section 6.
These sharing limits do not restrict earning income from permitted independent
professional services or delivering and commercializing Ordinary Work Products.

An eligible Individual may submit a contribution for inclusion only to the
extent that the Individual controls the necessary rights and identifies human
expression, AI assistance and third-party components. For the rights actually
held, the contributor grants the verified project rights holder a non-exclusive,
worldwide, royalty-free right to review, reproduce, modify, incorporate and
distribute the contribution as part of the Skill under this same License.
The contributor also offers eligible downstream Individuals the rights in that
contribution under this same License. This is not an assignment or permission
to relicense under other terms.

Submission through GitHub additionally requires authority for the actual
applicable platform grants over that submission; this License does not supply
missing platform rights or cancel GitHub's terms. Do not submit a contribution
with unresolved employer, client, joint-author or upstream rights. A personal
account is not proof of title. Separately authorized inclusion of employer-owned
expression does not authorize employees to operate the Skill for their employer.
No contribution grants an Organization operational rights to the whole Skill.

No contribution is accepted automatically. Lawful reading, platform functionality
and statutory exceptions remain preserved under Section 6.

## 6. Public reading, platform rights, and legal exceptions

Individuals and Organizations may read material lawfully made public. Public
visibility does not itself grant organizational Operational Use or a commercial
license to the Skill. Rights required by applicable hosting-platform terms,
including viewing and platform-native forking where applicable, and mandatory
statutory exceptions are unaffected. No clause purports to revoke rights that
the Licensor has granted to a platform or its users under those terms.

A platform-native fork does not by itself authorize deployment, corporate API
use, off-platform redistribution, or other uses outside the applicable platform
rights and this License. The extent of platform rights must be checked against
the terms applicable to that release and account; this text cannot narrow them.

This License does not claim exclusive rights in unprotected ideas, facts,
general methods, public-domain content, or independently created material. It
does not override fair use, fair dealing, quotation rights, or other mandatory
exceptions. Contractual effect beyond copyright, including assent and
enforceability, requires jurisdiction-specific review; merely reading a public
page is not asserted to create a separate binding contract.

## 7. Third parties, customer data, and ownership

Third-party works remain under their own rights and licenses; they are not
relicensed by this License. Citations do not authorize redistribution of papers,
books, datasets, code, or attachments. No representation is made that all
AI-generated expression is copyrightable or exclusively owned by the Licensor.
The grant covers only rights actually held and identified in the rights manifest.

Users must have lawful authority to process and disclose customer materials,
respect confidentiality and data protection obligations, and check rights in
their deliverables. No customer data, credentials, or private archives must be
submitted merely to demonstrate license compliance. Contributions require
separate confirmation of the contributor's rights and permission to include
them under the adopted terms; submitting a contribution does not transfer title.

## 8. Term, noncompliance, and reinstatement

The grant lasts for the applicable copyright term while its
conditions are met; later license versions do not automatically replace the
version validly received. There is no general right to withdraw a compliant
grant arbitrarily. Rights under this License terminate upon material violation
of its conditions, subject to mandatory law. A violating user must stop the
unauthorized activity and remove unauthorized operational copies under that
user's control. Statutory/platform rights and separately valid rights are
unaffected.

Reinstatement requires the Licensor's written confirmation after remediation;
no automatic cure or reinstatement is provided. Termination does not impose this
License on previously lawful Ordinary Work Products or revoke a customer's
independent rights in them. Mandatory notice, service, retention and remedy
requirements under applicable law remain unaffected; this section does not
require destruction of a copy that the law requires to be retained.

